WEBVTT

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:11.010
This story is a work of fiction. All persons and organizations are imagined. 
The kabaddi and game rules which appear in this anime are drawn from the original work.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:09.240
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:14.660
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:16.460
Kabaddi...

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.160
Okay, that's two points!

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:19.540
Hey!

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.510
Couldn't you see I was going for the tackle?

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.340
You were in the back, Yoigoshi! 
Shouldn't you have moved?

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.080
Quit fighting in the middle of practice.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.560
Isn't there some kind of secret 
to defense? Some trick?

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.050
Well...

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:36.050
With defense, you want 
to picture "fish herding."

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:37.640
Fish herding?

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.450
For example, if you came for me,

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:42.610
someone would come from 
behind, and "wham!"

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:44.520
Hold on! What's "wham" supposed to mean?

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.370
At any rate, if you can catch them, 
you can take them down.

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:50.320
I'm not like you!

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.940
Well, until things start shaping up,

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:56.450
<b>2nd-Years</b>

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:56.450
<b>1st-Years</b>

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:56.450
let's keep practicing two-on-two like this.

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:58.500
"Shaping up"?

00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.980
First-years versus second-years.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:03.040
Losers clean the mat and tidy up.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:43.050
<b>2nd-Years</b>

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:43.050
<b>1st-Years</b>

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:47.120
Into the
\h\h\h\h\hBurning World

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:46.160
We got thrashed.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:49.060
Look, do you guys know why you lost?

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:53.170
Because he keeps getting in my way!

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:56.570
I-Isn't it because Yoigoshi's 
defense keeps failing?

00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:03.200
<b>2nd-Years</b>

00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:03.200
<b>1st-Years</b>

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:59.410
Kabaddi is a sport played empty-handed.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:03.200
The rules are simple. The gap in experience 
between you is only about a year.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.460
Plus, you two are probably faster than them.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.160
<b>2nd-Years</b>

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.160
<b>1st-Years</b>

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.160
So, why...

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:08.710
did you get so overwhelmingly trounced?

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:12.420
Is it really okay for us to leave first?

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:13.780
Yup! Good work today!

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:16.430
Oh, but before you go, just one thing...

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:18.160
Say something to provoke them.

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:20.090
<b>Uhh...</b>

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.440
M-Man, you're nothing special.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:26.890
At this rate, I'd be better off 
playing against a scarecrow.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:28.720
Y-You don't have enough muscle.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.230
<b>Conserve
Water</b>

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:32.640
Damn it...

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:36.980
Yeah... Being told you're worse 
than a scarecrow is a shock.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:39.440
It's obvious that Iura made them say that!

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.080
Really?

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:43.450
The thing I'm angry about

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:45.820
is that the only reason 
I can think of for that rout

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:49.700
is a lack of teamwork!

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.310
Why does that make you angry?

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:57.210
Because it means that, to win, 
I need to work together with you!

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:02.560
You attack solo. Even if you fail, 
you only concede one point.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:04.340
But defense is different.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:06.140
Not being able to score is one thing,

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:09.320
but if things go badly, a lot 
of points can be taken at once.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:13.090
We can't keep running into each 
other and going off alone to tackle.

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:16.360
We have to think of a way to 
understand each others' movements.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.730
For example, if we want to dodge right,

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:22.400
we can say, "I'm dodging right!"
 Then we'd know!

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.740
I mean, the defense can talk, so...

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:28.030
Oh! No, that wouldn't work! 
The other team would hear, right?

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:30.960
That's it!

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:32.760
Huh?

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:36.750
<b>2nd-Years</b>

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:36.750
<b>1st-Years</b>

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.430
Kabaddi... Kabaddi!

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:42.090
One!

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:43.590
Three!

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:47.620
Sorry, Yoigoshi!

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.350
Listen better, idiot!

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:51.220
<i>Those numbers...</i>

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:53.640
<i>I see.</i>

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.530
We'll head out first!

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:01.280
Dang it.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:03.080
Thank you!

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:07.950
What they were doing today... 
Those were signs, weren't they?

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.030
Seemed like it.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:11.540
Okay.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:12.890
Let's go.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:16.040
Gymnasium 1

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.040
You're too fast! Hold up a minute!

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:18.300
Are you off to practice your signs?

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.970
You could tell we were doing signs?

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.530
Keep it a secret from the others.

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:29.070
A secret? When they're used right in 
front of you, you can't help but notice.

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:30.860
They were a suggestion 
from Yoigoshi, I take it?

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:33.690
Huh? Oh. We thought it up together.

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:36.120
I see. It's not bad.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.430
At the very least, you're doing 
better than in the beginning.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:40.610
Signs?

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:43.260
Yeah. For three things.

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:47.280
Dodge right. Dodge left. Go for the tackle.

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:50.270
I'll use numbers to issue these three orders.

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:52.600
Numbers, huh?

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:59.290
When it comes to strategy and evasion methods, 
Yoigoishi is first-rate, after all.

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:05.460
I only noticed recently, but the 
thing Yoigoshi is the most amazing at

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.800
is in a totally different place!

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:09.520
...is how it will go.

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:11.900
You're really amazing.

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:13.850
Going this far in a practice 
match within the team.

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:15.720
That's got nothing to do with it.

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:18.380
Regardless of who the opponents may be,

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:21.530
you're expected to give your
 utmost in every match.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:25.580
Huh?

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:32.440
Hey!

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:34.550
What took you so long?

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:41.100
It's crowded again today.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.860
It's a shortcut to my usual bento place.

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:47.180
And the path is narrow, so it's perfect 
for practicing evading people.

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:50.850
Rule 1: Do not come into contact with anyone.

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:52.310
Two is about speed.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:54.550
The half-priced bento will sell out quickly.

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:57.810
<b>Mega Portion</b>

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:57.810
<b>Great
Value</b>

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:57.810
<b>Half-Price</b>

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:57.810
It's not healthy to only eat stuff like that.

00:06:58.270 --> 00:06:59.970
Just follow me.

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:02.050
Don't forget the signs 
I taught you yesterday!

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:02.810
Got it!

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:05.630
Kabaddi is fought in close combat.

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:08.070
What we want is a hair's-breadth evasion,

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:11.450
and to maintain a stance 
that allows for a quick tackle.

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:13.330
How many times did you run 
into someone yesterday?

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:14.660
I grazed someone four times!

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.580
After you dodge, imagine yourself tackling!

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:18.840
I know!

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:22.850
Sorry! I made a mis—

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:24.540
Stay focused!

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:27.880
We made it with no "struggle."

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:30.140
You should at least finish with style.

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:35.290
After the break, we'll have a match.

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:37.260
Hey, Shin!

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:40.690
You played baseball through 
middle school, right?

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.540
What kind of guys did you have 
as your juniors on the team?

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:46.810
Mostly, there were those who 
were earnest and idolized you,

00:07:46.810 --> 00:07:48.730
or those who saw you as the 
competition. One of the two.

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:49.990
Really...

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:54.970
I like the guys who see you
 as the competition. They're fun.

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:56.380
I feel the same.

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:01.540
Man... We have some good junior 
members here, don't we?

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:04.460
<b>2nd-Years</b>

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:04.460
<b>1st-Years</b>

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:04.460
Second-years on offense. Commence play!

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:07.130
Now, my little juniors.

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:10.130
What will you do for me today?

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.130
<b>Raider
Misumi Kyohei</b>

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:12.400
Don't forget what we each have to do!

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:13.880
<b>Defense First-Years</b>

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:13.880
G-Got it!

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:16.730
<i>While one defenseman draws off the raider,</i>

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:19.590
<i>the other cuts off the 
raider's line of escape.</i>

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:20.240
<b>Line of Escape</b>

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:23.630
<i>First, I'll act as a decoy 
and lure the raider!</i>

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:26.400
I know he's working to lure him, but...

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.400
isn't that too close?

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.420
Kabaddi!

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:32.900
<i>He can evade even at this close a range?</i>

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:34.880
<i>Come on. Target me.</i>

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:37.930
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:37.910
<i>I'll chip away at your oxygen and 
keep you from scoring any points!</i>

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:40.910
<i>A normal decoy wouldn't 
be able to be that close.</i>

00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:43.120
<i>That's a feat only a monster can pull off.</i>

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:45.680
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:46.420
Five!

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:47.410
Got it!

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:51.080
<i>Man, those signs! Azemichi can dodge, too?</i>

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:53.880
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:53.880
All right!

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:56.140
<i>The evasion expert...</i>

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:59.930
<i>Yoigoishi's instincts are being 
transmitted perfectly to Azemichi.</i>

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:04.430
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.240
<i>Guess there's no helping it.</i>

00:09:02.710 --> 00:09:05.980
<i>I'll just have to make use 
of my defense experience...</i>

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:08.520
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:09.020
<i>This is how a raider herds fish into a net!</i>

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:11.530
<i>I'll run both of you into 
the side of the court!</i>

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:12.650
Kabaddi!

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:13.420
Four!

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:17.570
<i>Th-They aren't running into each other 
anymore! In just these few days?</i>

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:18.950
Kabaddi...

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.530
That's the first time we got away!

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:24.640
Without a tackle, we don't get points.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:28.970
We're just getting started!

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:37.550
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:37.550
Yoigoshi, you're a sharp one.

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:39.290
Haven't you figured out

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:42.720
the best way to work in sync?

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:46.120
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:46.120
<i>You're telling me my signs 
are inferior to a chain?</i>

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:49.300
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:48.810
Our evasions are succeeding.

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:52.610
<i>The chains...</i>

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:54.280
<i>are broken?</i>

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.370
<i>He's coming for the tackle solo!</i>

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:58.620
<i>But if he's alone, I can 
deflect him with my hand.</i>

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:00.450
<i>Here's a question for you, Yoigoshi.</i>

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:04.070
<i>When one defender, me, has both hands free...</i>

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:06.820
<i>what should the other defender be doing?</i>

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:13.100
<i>Letting go of his hand was a
 sign to go for a tackle?</i>

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:16.590
Oh, man...

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:18.970
<b>1st-Year Team   Yoigoshi
Raid Failed   1 Point Conceded</b>

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:21.820
Don't worry about it, Yoigoshi!

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:23.970
We'll get it back on defense!

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:26.960
I'll go.

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:28.690
What is wrong with your raid?

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:32.240
With that performance, 
they'll never see the flaw in their signs.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:36.940
<b>2nd-Year Team
Raider/Date</b>

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:40.320
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:37.980
<i>Date, huh?</i>

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:40.320
<i>He's slow, so he's easier to catch, but...</i>

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:43.450
<i>if he isn't taken down completely, 
he'll drag you all the way to his territory.</i>

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:47.180
<i>To get him, we need to lure 
him to the edge of the court.</i>

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:49.310
Fifty-five!

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:50.160
Got it!

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:53.460
Here we go! The two of us 
will simultaneously tackle—

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:56.680
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:01.890
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:03.000
kabaddi...

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.390
<b>2nd-Year Team   Date
Raid Successful   2 Points</b>

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:08.510
So their timing really is off 
when they go in to tackle?

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:09.760
It's pretty much simultaneous,

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:12.100
but you can shake them off 
when they come one at a time.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:14.630
Time to attack!

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:17.370
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:16.910
<i>Those signs.</i>

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:19.640
<i>They are absolutely working for evasion.</i>

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:22.820
<i>Yoigoshi's instincts are saving Azemichi.</i>

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:26.590
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:29.730
<i>And his raids are starting to look good.</i>

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:33.580
<b>1st-Years</b>

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:33.580
<b>2nd-Years</b>

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:33.580
<i>But he's never had to 
"take someone down" before.</i>

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:35.340
You're too slow!

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:40.170
<i>On this small court, the split second it 
takes to confirm a sign will prove deadly.</i>

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:43.070
You okay?

00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:45.700
You've been calling all through 
both attack and defense.

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:46.740
Shut up.

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:49.180
All you need to do is follow my orders.

00:11:50.030 --> 00:11:53.270
<i>Damn it, this is why I hate having 
to coordinate plays with others.</i>

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:58.690
<i>No one shows up in the place 
I want to receive my pass...</i>

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:01.820
<i>and a pass never comes to 
me when I want it, either.</i>

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:04.770
<i>Not like that. You're too slow.</i>

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:06.700
<i>That's not enough. This isn't working.</i>

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:10.580
<i>That's why coordinating plays is stupid.</i>

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:13.210
<b>2nd-Year Team
Raider/Date</b>

00:12:12.050 --> 00:12:14.710
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:14.710
Four!

00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:16.210
<i>Oh, no!</i>

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:19.870
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:24.600
That was a mistake in 
Yoigoshi's orders, right?

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:26.470
Did you figure out their signs?

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:28.750
Blast it! I'll get it back—

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:30.470
Next, I'll raid, okay?

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:32.710
You... What do you think you're doing?

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:35.630
I mean, you've been getting 
to do all the raids.

00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:38.570
That's because I'm faster!

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:40.610
Follow the plan!

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:43.980
I'm not some machine made just for you.

00:12:43.980 --> 00:12:45.110
What?

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:48.490
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi!

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:47.980
Calm down, Yoigoshi.

00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:49.710
Iura...

00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:57.250
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi!

00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:51.400
It's your weakness!

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:53.560
Your logic and abilities are above average.

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:56.840
And, up until now, you've managed to get 
by on your own. That's your weakness!

00:12:57.250 --> 00:13:04.260
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi!

00:12:57.990 --> 00:12:59.930
What's wrong with that?

00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:01.540
I never said there was 
anything wrong with it.

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:04.260
But it is unmistakably a weakness.

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:08.910
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi!

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:08.330
You haven't really watched your teammate 
fight your opponents, have you?

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:12.750
Somehow, the defense's stance...

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:14.270
is it lower than when I went?

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:17.270
Kabaddi! Kabaddi!

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:18.320
He got me!

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:19.530
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:22.050
Kabaddi, kabaddi!

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.320
<b>1st Year Team   Azemichi
Raid Successful   2 points</b>

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:28.320
<b>1st-Years</b>

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:28.320
<b>2nd-Years</b>

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:28.320
We got two points back!

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:31.450
Did you see that, Yoigoshi?

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:34.760
To think I've learned something 
else from an idiot...

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:35.460
Huh?

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:39.460
<b>2nd Year Team
Raider/Misumi</b>

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.850
We'll stop them this time!

00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:41.580
Misumi...

00:13:42.140 --> 00:13:43.840
I'm not sure, but those signs...

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:47.980
I think I understand all the movement 
patterns the numbers indicate.

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:51.030
Even numbers. Odd numbers. Double digits.

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:53.310
He's giving orders for three patterns.

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:55.770
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:57.990
Kabaddi! Kabaddi!

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:00.770
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:01.350
Four!

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:03.880
That's the sign for "right"!

00:14:07.350 --> 00:14:09.030
<i>Huh? The opposite?</i>

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:11.850
<i>He got tricked by the fake sign!</i>

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:13.700
<i>I thought they'd have them 
figured out around now!</i>

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:17.760
I'll use numbers to issue these three orders.

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:18.830
Numbers, huh?

00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:24.340
At least, that's how we'll make it look,
 and we'll use different signs.

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:27.840
The numbers are a fake 
to hide the real signs.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:31.480
I'll use my fingers to give 
you the signs. Watch closely.

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:34.720
So, the fingers were the 
real signs after all.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:37.560
<i>And the thing you must take hold of 
after a hair's-breadth evasion is...</i>

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:39.480
<i>the pivot leg holding all 
the person's body weight!</i>

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:43.040
<i>Until now, we've been aiming for 
the body since it's easier to grab,</i>

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:46.000
<i>but to stop a raid, 
you should take a lower stance...</i>

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:48.110
<i>because grabbing the legs is best!</i>

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:52.120
<i>If I can grab his leg, 
Azemichi can tackle him!</i>

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:56.620
<i>Oh, no! I forgot to give him a sign!</i>

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:13.970
<b>2nd-Year Team   Misumi
Raid Failed   1 Point Conceded</b>

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:16.810
How did you...

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:19.090
I'm not some machine.

00:15:19.090 --> 00:15:21.980
I can't move exactly according to orders,

00:15:22.510 --> 00:15:26.440
but I watch my teammates closely and I think.

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:29.490
Earlier, you said you 
"learned something," right?

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:30.280
Huh?

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:34.700
The last time you said that, 
you pulled off something insane.

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:37.240
That's why, for me it sounded like...

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:40.740
"I'm gonna do something crazy. Follow me!"

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:42.410
That's what I heard, loud and clear!

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:45.560
<i>I didn't say that...</i>

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:46.870
<i>I never said anything...</i>

00:15:50.490 --> 00:15:51.420
<i>What is this?</i>

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:53.100
<i>What is it?</i>

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:56.560
<i>What is this feeling?</i>

00:15:57.510 --> 00:16:00.520
<b>1st-Years</b>

00:15:57.510 --> 00:16:00.520
<b>2nd-Years</b>

00:15:58.130 --> 00:15:59.390
Yeah.

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:04.020
That feeling gives you goosebumps, right?

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:09.810
We've known that feeling for a long time now.

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:12.700
And what's beyond that, too!

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:14.950
Beyond this...

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:20.160
<b>1st Year Team
Raider/Yoigoshi</b>

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:20.160
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:22.670
Kabaddi!

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:23.950
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:29.550
<b>1st Year Team   Yoigoshi
Raid Successful   2 Points</b>

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:33.880
<b>1st-Years</b>

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:33.880
<b>2nd-Years</b>

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:31.530
Three points down.

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:33.040
We can do this, Yoigoshi!

00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:33.880
Yeah.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:37.890
Not just "yeah!" Come on! High five! Right here!

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:40.270
Hurry up. We're on defense.

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:41.980
Why can't you just be honest with yourself?

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:46.400
If getting fired up freaks you out...

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.250
you'll never win.

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:49.400
<b>2nd-Year Team
Raider/Misumi</b>

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:52.760
He looks like a beast.

00:16:53.390 --> 00:16:56.620
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:58.870
<i>I've used a lot of metaphors 
to explain kabaddi.</i>

00:16:56.620 --> 00:17:00.030
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:03.370
<i>Tag and combat sports... 
Neither of those are wrong.</i>

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:03.370
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:06.720
<i>A team sport played empty-handed, kabaddi.</i>

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:10.000
<i>Its origins lie in hunting.</i>

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:13.400
<i>The skills an unarmed human 
needs to capture a wild beast</i>

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:15.380
<i>matured and developed into 
this, or so they say.</i>

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:17.770
<i>Which means that kabaddi</i>

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:19.400
<i>goes back to the origins 
of living creatures...</i>

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:22.400
<i>It's a sport that awakens primal instincts!</i>

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:25.180
You can't lie.

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:27.800
It's written all over your face.

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:30.340
Kabaddi!

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:31.070
Two!

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:35.130
<i>My breath... I can't shout anymore...</i>

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:38.560
<i>Maybe just the hand signs will be enough?</i>

00:17:38.560 --> 00:17:41.580
<i>No. Even just giving signs is tough.</i>

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:45.210
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:45.630
<i>Why am I trying so hard at this anyway?</i>

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:47.500
<i>I hate sports.</i>

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:51.090
<b>1st Half</b>

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:51.090
<b>2nd Half</b>

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:51.090
<b>Overtime
1st Half 2nd Half</b>

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:51.090
<b>Total</b>

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:50.200
<i>Is that really true?</i>

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:54.050
<i>When I played soccer, 
all that stuff happened.</i>

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:58.050
<i>Then why isn't it "I hate soccer" 
instead of "I hate sports"?</i>

00:17:58.370 --> 00:18:00.300
<i>Because I fought with my teammates, right?</i>

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:05.810
<b>Yoigoshi the Unstoppable, Scores 4 Goals in Bad Weather</b>

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:05.810
<b>Is promotion to the Youth league near?! We're closing in on the details!</b>

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:03.010
<i>There may have been some problems,</i>

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:05.320
<i>but as long as we produced results,
 all that could be ignored.</i>

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:09.630
<i>Just like my teammates said, 
as long as we got results,</i>

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:11.310
<i>there was no need to try hard.</i>

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:16.990
<i>As soon as I thought of that as the 
correct path, sports felt boring.</i>

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:20.370
<i>Everyone around me reeked 
of lies. I hated it.</i>

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:25.830
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:23.280
<i>Hold on!</i>

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:26.090
<i>That makes it seem like what
 I wanted was friends!</i>

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:26.500
Kabaddi!

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:31.000
Don't space out on me, Yoigoshi!

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:35.210
You're expected to give your
 utmost in every match, right?

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:37.100
You weren't lying, right?

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:38.720
That's right.

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:44.330
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:41.260
<i>It's no lie!</i>

00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:44.300
<i>When you include the time for 
switching offense and defense,</i>

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:47.000
<i>we probably only have 
once chance left to raid.</i>

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:47.480
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:51.690
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:49.690
<i>We need to gain points on defense!</i>

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:51.290
Azemichi!

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:54.010
<i>What's with this formation?</i>

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:55.020
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:18:54.010 --> 00:18:55.690
<i>It's obvious they don't want me getting back.</i>

00:18:56.510 --> 00:18:58.670
<i>I'll look for an opening and touch Yoigoshi.</i>

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:01.170
<i>On the way back, I'll tag 
Azemichi for the second point.</i>

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:05.100
<i>So you are coming in, 
you super-aggressive decoy!</i>

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:08.250
<i>But really... You're underestimating 
me a little too much!</i>

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:08.250
Kabaddi!

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:12.810
<i>If Azemichi gets close, then I can 
escape to the right. No problem.</i>

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:17.330
<i>Giving those orders and doing all 
the raiding has exhausted you.</i>

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:19.760
<i>Can you really keep dodging at this distance?</i>

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:25.510
Thanks for not running, Senpai.

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:27.160
Misumi!

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:31.240
<i>Oh, no! I took my eyes off him for a second!</i>

00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:33.400
<i>But, just like I thought, if I go right...</i>

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:35.400
<i>Too bad.</i>

00:19:35.850 --> 00:19:38.100
<i>This is a dead end, too!</i>

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:50.330
Kabaddi...

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:53.000
<i>He's going over? This can't be happening!</i>

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:56.210
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi!

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:57.500
<i>No one...</i>

00:19:57.730 --> 00:20:00.680
<i>Not even Azemichi expected that chain...</i>

00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:03.510
<i>Even then... Even with that...</i>

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:07.030
<i>We still couldn't stop him?</i>

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:08.350
<b>2nd-Year Team   Misumi
 Raid Successful   2 Points</b>

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:09.850
<b>1st-Years</b>

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:09.850
<b>2nd-Years</b>

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:14.360
A team-up made overnight 
isn't gonna work on me.

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:19.280
<i>He got me.</i>

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:20.940
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:23.780
<i>Do I just need to work on getting 
tougher like all of you?</i>

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:26.290
<i>Or, should I learn to be more like Iura?</i>

00:20:26.760 --> 00:20:27.600
<i>I don't know.</i>

00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:31.120
I'll go raid.

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:33.000
Y-You sure you're good to go, Yoigoshi?

00:20:34.020 --> 00:20:35.710
We've got one more turn on defense.

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:37.730
Make sure you've got some stamina left.

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:39.700
We need your strength for defense.

00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:45.660
<i>Man... What I went and said 
just now isn't like me at all.</i>

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:48.760
<i>It's been a long time since 
I was this close to my limits...</i>

00:20:49.710 --> 00:20:54.650
<i>That's right. When you're short on 
oxygen, your vision gets blurry.</i>

00:20:54.650 --> 00:20:56.020
<i>I'd forgotten.</i>

00:20:57.010 --> 00:20:58.640
<i>This world...</i>

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:02.190
<i>This burning world...</i>

00:21:03.180 --> 00:21:05.200
<i>It feels so good!</i>

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:08.670
All right! Let's stop him, Shin!

00:21:08.670 --> 00:21:09.160
Yeah!

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:16.090
End of match!

00:21:16.090 --> 00:21:18.570
With a score of 22 to 18, 
the second-years win!

00:21:20.510 --> 00:21:21.760
Water!

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:23.370
A four-point gap, huh?

00:21:23.370 --> 00:21:24.130
Damn it!

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:27.850
Even though you got a point 
back at the end, Yoigoshi...

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:30.640
No. Before thinking about 
that, our defense is still—

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:34.160
What are you trying to do?!

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.040
Make sure your body doesn't get cold.

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:38.650
Huh? This isn't my jacket—

00:21:39.130 --> 00:21:41.070
Nope. It's yours.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:44.600
Hey, Yoigoshi.

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:47.160
Kabaddi is fun, isn't it?

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:52.160
It's boring.

00:21:53.210 --> 00:21:55.050
If I can't win, it's boring!

00:21:56.480 --> 00:21:58.210
Just one more step.

00:21:58.210 --> 00:21:59.450
Always, over and over.

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:02.270
I'm going to get past that "one more step."

00:22:02.670 --> 00:22:05.550
If this coordinating with teammates 
thing is necessary to win,

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:07.140
then I guess I have no choice.

00:22:07.140 --> 00:22:08.650
I'll be your teammate.

00:22:09.890 --> 00:22:12.680
In that case, Yoigoshi-kun, 
allow me to formally say...

00:22:14.070 --> 00:22:16.620
welcome to the kabaddi team.

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:54.250
<b>Next Time
"The Strongest Raider"</b>

00:23:49.500 --> 00:23:52.590
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:52.590
Next time, "The Strongest Raider!"

00:23:52.590 --> 00:23:53.340
Kabaddi!
